    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0513" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/11–1248:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-12T16:00:00+01:00">November 12,
                            1948—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5847. Referring to his protest against recent action taken by military commanders
                    at Frankfurt concerning the Ruhr, Schuman
                    said he realizes full well that a good part of French policy towards Germany is
                    not realistic (but the French people in general do not realize that); he knows
                    furthermore that France will have to abandon at least some of her positions in
                    connection with Germany. He said also that in no event would he accept Russian
                    participation in any form in the Ruhr.</p>
                <p>What he did resent more than anything else he added was the “timing” of the
                    Frankfurt “affair”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
